codex
The defect is localized: `build_plan` currently treats every manifest-only path as safe to write, while `apply_update` creates backup/progress state before any target collision check. I’m adding a preflight blocker that uses lexical existence checks (including broken symlinks) and rejects non-directory ancestors, then extending the existing public smoke fixture with the required no-mutation and late-collision regressions.
